<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Hague</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Den Haag, 's-Gravenhage</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hague is a city in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> and the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> government, parliament and monarchy, although <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a> is the constitutional capital. It grew around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/binnenhof">Binnenhof</a>, the castle begun by the counts of Holland in the 13th century, and from the 16th century hosted the States General of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>. It is home to international courts including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/international-court-of-justice">International Court of Justice</a> and the International Criminal Court.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/the-hague.jpg" alt="The Hague" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zairon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Den_Haag_Skyline_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
